  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'Players ante; dealer deals five cards each (two face down, three face up) and places three face-up cards plus the deck as the buy row (prices 1, 2, 3, 4 units from left to deck). Three buying rounds: each player in turn may buy one card (discard one, pay price, take replacement), stand pat, or fold. Face-up bought cards are replaced from the deck. After each buying round, a betting round starts with the player showing the best hand. After the third betting round, surviving players declare high, low, or both; then showdown and the pot is split between high and low winners.',
    Player: 'Players ante; dealer deals five cards each (two face down, three face up) and places three face-up cards plus the deck as the buy row (prices 1, 2, 3, 4 units from left to deck). Three buying rounds: each player in turn may buy one card (discard one, pay price, take replacement), stand pat, or fold. Face-up bought cards are replaced from the deck. After each buying round, a betting round starts with the player showing the best hand. After the third betting round, surviving players declare high, low, or both; then showdown and the pot is split between high and low winners.',
    objective: 'Form the best five-card high hand, low hand, or both (declare high, low, or both). Win the pot by having the best hand at showdown or by making opponents fold.',
    gameplay: 'Players ante; dealer deals five cards each (two face down, three face up) and places three face-up cards plus the deck as the buy row (prices 1, 2, 3, 4 units from left to deck). Three buying rounds: each player in turn may buy one card (discard one, pay price, take replacement), stand pat, or fold. Face-up bought cards are replaced from the deck. After each buying round, a betting round starts with the player showing the best hand. After the third betting round, surviving players declare high, low, or both; then showdown and the pot is split between high and low winners.',
    keyRules: [
      'Five cards each: two hole cards, three upcards.',
      'Buy row: three face-up cards (1, 2, 3 units) and top of deck (4 units); unit equals ante.',
      'Three buying rounds, each followed by a betting round.',
      'At your turn in a buying round: buy a card (discard one, pay price, replace), stand pat, or fold.',
      'Player showing best hand starts each betting round.',
      'High-low with declaration before showdown; high and low split the pot.',
